      "id": 1,
      "text": "Export earned its name from the coal that was once mined and shipped out of the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Export%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1911 Export became an independent borough, breaking away from Franklin Township, now part of Murrysville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://exportpennsylvania.com/export-historical-society/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Export Historical Society, born after a centennial celebration, safeguards the borough’s industrial past with photos and documents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://exportpennsylvania.com/export-historical-society/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Since 2016 the society has staged an annual event that highlights Export’s rich heritage and hopeful future.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://exportpennsylvania.com/export-historical-society/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Export hosts the Free Gospel Bible Institute, an international ministerial college established in 1958.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Export%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The State Library of Pennsylvania’s digital archives include Export’s local newspapers that reach back into the 18th century.",
